  "layout_html": "<p>30-byte header; each allocation adds 16 bytes. Entry offsets below describe the first entry.</p><table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"3\"><tr bgcolor=\"#E6A0AA\"><th>Byte</th><th>Field / source</th></tr><tr><td>1-2</td><td><b>Segment Identification</b><br>COBOL: FALIDENT-SEGMENT-ID<br>Constant: 57</td></tr><tr><td>3-4</td><td><b>Segment Length</b><br>COBOL: FALLNGTH-SEGMENT-LENGTH<br>30 header bytes + 16 bytes per allocation (including the P/D/U redefines).</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><b>Flag Byte A</b><br>COBOL: FALFLAGA-FLAG-BYTE-A<br>Bit 0: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.ALC_SRC_CD<br>Bit 1: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.AUTOCLOS_PROC_IND<br>Bit 2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.MTHLVRSY_PROC_IND<br>Bits 3-6 reserved; bit 7 group-control generation has no verified DB2 source.<br>Bit 0: internally generated. Bit 1: automated closed-fund processing.<br>Bit 2 = 1 means monthliversary processing has NOT occurred since addition.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>Flag Byte U</b><br>COBOL: FALFLAGU-USER-FLAG-BYTE<br>User-reserved byte; displayed as an example.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><b>Segment Type</b><br>COBOL: FALTYPE-SEG-TYPE<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.FND_TRS_TYP_CD</td></tr><tr><td>8-9</td><td><b>Type Sequence</b><br>COBOL: FALTYSEQ-TYPE-SEQ<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.FND_ALC_SEQ_NBR<br>Join LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.FND_ALC_SEQ_NBR to LH_FND_ALC.FND_ALC_SEQ_NBR.</td></tr><tr><td>10-13</td><td><b>Last Allocation Change Date</b><br>COBOL: FALLCGDT-LAST-CHANGE-DATE<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.LST_ALC_CHG_DT (non-C sets)<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.CRG_DED_ALC_EFF_DT (C charge-deduction sets)</td></tr><tr><td>14-15</td><td><b>Sweep From Fund</b><br>COBOL: FALSWPFF-SWEEP-FROM-FUND<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.SWP_FROM_FUND</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td><b>Allocation Method</b><br>COBOL: FALALLOM-ALLOCATION-METHOD<br>DB2: LH_FND_TRS_ALC_SET.ALC_MTH_CD</td></tr><tr><td>17-28</td><td><b>Cyberlife Reserved</b><br>COBOL: FALRSRVD-CYBERTEK-RESERVED</td></tr><tr><td>29-30</td><td><b>Number of Allocations</b><br>COBOL: FALALNUM-NUMBER-OF-ALLOCATIONS<br>Derived: count of LH_FND_ALC rows for this allocation type and set sequence.<br>SEG_IDX_NBR orders the entries; the workbook swaps its description with FND_ALC_SEQ_NBR.</td></tr><tr><td>31-33</td><td><b>Allocation Filler</b><br>COBOL: FILLER</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td><b>Allocation From/To Indicator</b><br>COBOL: FALFRMTO-FROM-TO-INDICATOR<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_ALC_DIR_CD</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td><b>Allocation Exclusion Indicator</b><br>COBOL: FALEXCLD-EXCLUDE-INDICATOR<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_XCL_IND</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td><b>Allocation Coverage Phase</b><br>COBOL: FALCOVPH-ASSOC-COV-PHASE<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.COV_PHA_NBR</td></tr><tr><td>37-38</td><td><b>Allocation Fund Identification</b><br>COBOL: FALFNDID-FUND-ID<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_ID_CD</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td><b>Allocation Value Type</b><br>COBOL: FALALVAL-ALLOC-VALUE<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.ALC_VAL_TYP_CD</td></tr><tr><td>40-46</td><td><b>Fund Allocation Units</b><br>COBOL: FALALUNI-FUND-ALLOC-UNITS<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_ALC_UNT_QTY<br>Type U: 13 packed digits, 4 decimal places.</td></tr><tr><td>40-45</td><td><b>Fund Allocation Dollars</b><br>COBOL: FALALDOL-FUND-ALLOC-DOL<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_ALC_AMT<br>Type D: 11 packed digits, 2 decimal places.</td></tr><tr><td>40-42</td><td><b>Fund Allocation Percent</b><br>COBOL: FALALPER-FUND-ALLOC-PCT<br>DB2: LH_FND_ALC.FND_ALC_PCT<br>Type P: 5 packed digits, 2 decimal places.</td></tr></table>"
}
